@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Foderliste";
    ViewData["TitleEn"] = "Food list";
}

<div class="wrap section guide-intro">
    <div class="actions no-print">
        <a class="btn btn--quiet" asp-page="/Pasningsguide" data-en="Back to the care guide">Tilbage til pasningsguiden</a>
        <button type="button" class="btn" data-print data-en="Print or save as PDF">Udskriv / gem som PDF</button>
    </div>
    <div class="section-head">
        <h1 data-en="Guinea pig food list">Marsvins foderliste</h1>
        <p data-en="What's safe every day, what's fine in small amounts, and what to never give.">
            Hvad der er sikkert hver dag, hvad der er fint i små mængder, og
            hvad du aldrig skal give.
        </p>
        <p data-en="Rotate a few different items from the daily list rather than feeding the same two vegetables every day — variety is what actually gets them the full spread of nutrients, not any single &quot;superfood&quot; vegetable.">
            Skift mellem et par forskellige ting fra dagslisten i stedet for
            at give de samme to grøntsager hver dag — variation er det, der
            reelt giver dem det fulde spekter af næringsstoffer, ikke én bestemt "supergrøntsag".
        </p>
        <p data-en="Covers vegetables, fruit, and — since guinea pig owners often pick greens straight from the garden — the weeds, flowers, and hedge plants that come up most often as either a good find or a real risk.">
            Dækker grøntsager, frugt, og — siden marsvineejere ofte plukker
            grønt direkte fra haven — de ukrudtsplanter, blomster og
            hækplanter, der oftest dukker op, enten som et godt fund eller som en reel risiko.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap guide-article">
        <div class="callout food-callout food-callout--safe">
            <h2 data-en="Safe, every day">Sikkert, hver dag</h2>
            <ul class="food-grid">
                <li><strong data-en="Hay">Hø</strong><span data-en="Unlimited, always available">Ubegrænset, altid tilgængeligt</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Guinea-pig-specific pellets">Marsvine-specifikt pillefoder</strong><span data-en="A measured daily portion">En afmålt daglig portion</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Fresh water">Frisk vand</strong><span data-en="Checked daily, not just topped up">Tjekket dagligt, ikke bare fyldt op</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Bell pepper">Peberfrugt</strong><span data-en="High in vitamin C, especially red and yellow">Højt C-vitaminindhold, især rød og gul</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Cucumber">Agurk</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Romaine, rocket, lamb's lettuce">Romainesalat, rucola, feldsalat</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Tomato">Tomat</strong><span data-en="Flesh only - not the stem or leaves">Kun kødet - ikke stilk eller blade</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Broccoli">Broccoli</strong><span data-en="Small amounts - can cause gas">Små mængder - kan give luft i maven</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Celery">Selleri</strong><span data-en="Cut the stringy fibres first - a choking hazard otherwise">Fjern de seje tråde først - ellers kvælningsfare</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Courgette / squash">Squash / courgette</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Green beans">Grønne bønner</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Fresh dandelion greens">Friske mælkebøtteblade</strong><span data-en="From an unsprayed patch, not the roadside">Fra et sted der ikke er sprøjtet, ikke fra vejkanten</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Basil">Basilikum</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Coriander">Koriander</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Carrot tops (the leafy greens)">Gulerodstoppe (det grønne)</strong><span data-en="Often more nutritious than the root itself">Ofte mere nærende end selve roden</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Fennel, bulb and fronds">Fennikel, knold og top</strong><span data-en="A favourite for most guinea pigs">En favorit hos de fleste marsvin</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Bok choy / pak choi">Pak choi</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Radicchio and endive">Radicchio og julesalat</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Watercress">Brøndkarse</strong><span data-en="Peppery — some guinea pigs turn their nose up at it">Skarp smag - nogle marsvin bryder sig ikke om den</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Dill">Dild</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Oregano and thyme">Oregano og timian</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Mint">Mynte</strong><span data-en="Strong flavour — a little goes a long way">Kraftig smag - lidt rækker langt</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Radish tops (the leafy greens)">Radisetoppe (det grønne)</strong></li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="callout food-callout food-callout--moderate">
            <h2 data-en="Fine in small amounts, a couple of times a week">Fint i små mængder, et par gange om ugen</h2>
            <ul class="food-grid">
                <li><strong data-en="Carrot">Gulerod</strong><span data-en="High in sugar">Højt sukkerindhold</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Apple">Æble</strong><span data-en="No seeds - they contain trace cyanide">Uden kerner - de indeholder spor af cyanid</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Strawberry, banana, blueberry, raspberry">Jordbær, banan, blåbær, hindbær</strong><span data-en="High in sugar - treat-sized portions">Højt sukkerindhold - godbid-størrelse</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Dried dandelion">Tørret mælkebøtte</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Corn">Majs</strong><span data-en="Small amounts - high in starch">Små mængder - højt stivelsesindhold</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Peas">Ærter</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Beetroot">Rødbede</strong><span data-en="Can tint their urine red - harmless, but don't mistake it for blood">Kan farve urinen rød - harmløst, men forveksl det ikke med blod</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Pumpkin">Græskar</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Cabbage / white cabbage">Kål / hvidkål</strong><span data-en="Can cause gas">Kan give luft i maven</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Spinach and kale">Spinat og grønkål</strong><span data-en="High in calcium/oxalic acid - a couple of times a week, not daily">Højt i calcium/oxalsyre - et par gange om ugen, ikke dagligt</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Parsley">Persille</strong><span data-en="High in oxalic acid despite the vitamin C - the same reason as spinach">Højt i oxalsyre trods C-vitaminet - samme grund som spinat</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Citrus (e.g. orange)">Citrusfrugt (fx appelsin)</strong><span data-en="Can irritate the mouth in larger amounts">Kan irritere munden i større mængder</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Pear">Pære</strong><span data-en="No seeds, same reason as apple">Uden kerner, samme grund som æble</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Melon (watermelon, cantaloupe)">Melon (vandmelon, cantaloupe)</strong><span data-en="High in sugar and water">Højt sukker- og vandindhold</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Grapes">Vindruer</strong><span data-en="Halved, seedless">Halveret, uden kerner</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Kiwi">Kiwi</strong><span data-en="High in vitamin C, but sugary and acidic">Rig på C-vitamin, men sukker- og syreholdig</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Mango and pineapple">Mango og ananas</strong><span data-en="High in sugar and acidity">Højt sukker- og syreindhold</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Cauliflower and Brussels sprouts">Blomkål og rosenkål</strong><span data-en="Can cause gas">Kan give luft i maven</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Swiss chard">Bladbeder</strong><span data-en="High in oxalic acid, the same reason as spinach">Højt i oxalsyre, samme grund som spinat</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Radish">Radise</strong><span data-en="Sharp flavour — small amounts">Skarp smag - små mængder</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Clover">Kløver</strong><span data-en="Can cause gas or bloat in large amounts">Kan give luft i maven eller oppustethed i store mængder</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Iceberg lettuce">Iceberg-salat</strong><span data-en="Not toxic, but mostly water and almost no nutrition - too much can cause diarrhoea">Ikke giftig, men mest vand og næsten ingen næringsværdi - for meget kan give diarré</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="callout food-callout food-callout--never">
            <h2 data-en="Never">Aldrig</h2>
            <ul class="food-grid">
                <li><strong data-en="Avocado">Avocado</strong><span data-en="Toxic to guinea pigs">Giftig for marsvin</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Onion, garlic, leek">Løg, hvidløg, porre</strong><span data-en="The whole allium family - damages red blood cells">Hele løg-familien - skader røde blodlegemer</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Chocolate">Chokolade</strong><span data-en="Toxic">Giftig</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Dairy products">Mejeriprodukter</strong><span data-en="Adult guinea pigs are lactose intolerant">Voksne marsvin er laktoseintolerante</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Rhubarb">Rabarber</strong><span data-en="Toxic - high in oxalic acid">Giftig - højt indhold af oxalsyre</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Nuts and seeds">Nødder og frø</strong><span data-en="Choking hazard, too much fat">Kvælningsfare, for meget fedt</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Green potato / potato sprouts">Grønne kartofler / kartoffeltop</strong><span data-en="Contains solanine - toxic">Indeholder solanin - giftigt</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Bread, pasta, meat and other human food">Brød, pasta, kød og andet menneskemad</strong><span data-en="Not built for a guinea pig's gut">Ikke bygget til et marsvins fordøjelse</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Mushrooms">Svampe</strong><span data-en="Can be toxic and are hard to tell apart safely">Kan være giftige og er svære at kende sikkert fra hinanden</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Dried or raw beans (e.g. kidney beans)">Tørrede eller rå bønner (fx kidneybønner)</strong><span data-en="Toxic uncooked - not the same as fresh green beans above">Giftige rå - ikke det samme som de friske grønne bønner ovenfor</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <article>
            <h2 data-en="From the garden">Fra haven</h2>
            <p data-en="Many owners pick greens for their guinea pigs straight from the garden. Only from a patch you know hasn't been sprayed, and never from the roadside - the same rule as the dandelion above.">
                Mange marsvineejere plukker grønt til deres marsvin direkte fra
                haven. Kun fra et sted du ved ikke er sprøjtet, og aldrig fra
                vejkanten - samme regel som mælkebøtten ovenfor.
            </p>
        </article>

        <div class="callout food-callout food-callout--safe">
            <h2 data-en="Safe">Sikkert</h2>
            <ul class="food-grid">
                <li><strong data-en="Dandelion (leaves and flower)">Mælkebøtte (blade og blomst)</strong><span data-en="See the safe list above">Se den sikre liste ovenfor</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Grass, fresh and unsprayed">Frisk, usprøjtet græs</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Plantain (the weed, not the banana relative)">Vejbred</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Chickweed">Fuglegræs</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Sow thistle">Svinemælk</strong></li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="callout food-callout food-callout--moderate">
            <h2 data-en="Fine in small amounts">I små mængder</h2>
            <ul class="food-grid">
                <li><strong data-en="Yarrow">Røllike</strong><span data-en="Strong aromatic oils - an occasional treat, not a staple">Kraftige aromatiske olier - en godbid en gang imellem, ikke en fast del af kosten</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Nettle, wilted or young leaves">Brændenælde, visnet eller unge blade</strong><span data-en="Wilt or chop it first - fresh nettle stings. High in calcium, the same reason as clover">Lad den visne eller hak den først - frisk nælde brænder. Højt calciumindhold, samme grund som kløver</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Rose petals and leaves">Roseblade og -kronblade</strong><span data-en="Thornless and unsprayed - a treat-sized amount">Uden torne og usprøjtet - godbid-størrelse</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Marigold (Calendula)">Morgenfrue</strong><span data-en="An edible flower - an occasional treat">En spiselig blomst - en godbid en gang imellem</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Sunflower leaves and petals">Solsikkeblade og -kronblade</strong><span data-en="The leaves and petals only - not the seeds, listed under Never">Kun bladene og kronbladene - ikke kernerne, nævnt under Aldrig</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Hibiscus">Hibiscus</strong><span data-en="An edible flower - an occasional treat">En spiselig blomst - en godbid en gang imellem</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="callout food-callout food-callout--never">
            <h2 data-en="Toxic, avoid">Giftigt, undgå</h2>
            <p data-en="Common in Danish gardens and hedges - worth knowing by sight before you let anything green come from outside.">
                Almindelige i danske haver og hække - værd at kunne kende på synet, før du lader noget grønt komme udefra.
            </p>
            <ul class="food-grid">
                <li><strong data-en="Foxglove">Fingerbøl</strong><span data-en="Toxic to the heart">Giftig for hjertet</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Lily of the valley">Liljekonval</strong><span data-en="Toxic to the heart">Giftig for hjertet</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Ivy">Vedbend</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Buttercup, fresh">Smørblomst, frisk</strong><span data-en="Irritates the mouth and gut">Irriterer mund og fordøjelse</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Rhododendron and azalea">Rhododendron og azalea</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Oleander">Oleander</strong><span data-en="Highly toxic">Meget giftig</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Yew">Taks</strong><span data-en="Highly toxic">Meget giftig</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Hemlock">Skarntyde</strong><span data-en="Highly toxic">Meget giftig</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Daffodil and tulip (bulbs and leaves)">Påskelilje og tulipan (løg og blade)</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Bracken fern">Ørnebregne</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Tomato and potato plant leaves and stems">Tomat- og kartoffelplantens blade og stængler</strong><span data-en="Not the ripe fruit itself, listed above">Ikke selve den modne frugt, nævnt ovenfor</span></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Privet">Liguster</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Boxwood">Buksbom</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Groundsel">Brandbæger</strong></li>
                <li><strong data-en="Hydrangea">Hortensia</strong></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
